WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.350
In .NET AI systems, policy filters first
screen options based on privacy rules,
required capabilities, and resource limits
like latency or cost, ensuring only
eligible choices proceed.

2
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:23.550
After filtering, the AI model or decision
component evaluates remaining options,
returning a structured choice along with a
confidence score indicating certainty in
that selection.

3
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:36.050
A confidence threshold can reject
uncertain results, triggering an explicit
fallback process that is observable and
never silently switches providers,
maintaining transparency and control.
